WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.154
Welcome to the first Project Kamp update video!

00:00:07.154 --> 00:00:11.085
So, these videos are basically just to keep 
progress of what we're doing.

00:00:11.085 --> 00:00:13.545
To make sure we&nbsp;archive it for ourselves.

00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:15.916
And also, for our family and friends to follow.

00:00:16.395 --> 00:00:19.261
We basically&nbsp;bought this big piece of land in Portugal!

00:00:19.261 --> 00:00:23.087
We're going to transform it into something,&nbsp;
to live and work in a more sustainable way.

00:00:23.566 --> 00:00:25.255
We don't really know where this is going...

00:00:25.255 --> 00:00:27.775
We have&nbsp;some sort of wild plans in our head.

00:00:27.775 --> 00:00:32.002
But, I guess that this is just to keep following that process.

00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:33.598
So, if&nbsp;you're interested, make sure to subscribe!

00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:36.460
If not, yeah, don't...

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.917
Overall, the videos are going to be very&nbsp;quick and rough.

00:00:39.479 --> 00:00:44.326
Because, we just want to make sure we actually 
do document it, and don't forget&nbsp;about it...

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.135
So, if you make it too complex,
I know we're not gonna do it in the end.

00:00:48.135 --> 00:00:52.685
We just&nbsp;have very little people around here,
 so we need to use our resources properly.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.789
So, yeah: first update!

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:58.486
Let me give you a quick tour of the land!

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.200
We're now walking down on&nbsp;the land, so this is all the land!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.861 --> 00:01:16.541
Above there as well actually, but there's&nbsp;
a bit less interesting things to show for now.

00:01:17.881 --> 00:01:21.049
This road is going down to the workspace,&nbsp;and the kitchen.

00:01:21.695 --> 00:01:28.566
We're first gonna have a look at the workspace,
 which is a bit hidden&nbsp;in the bushes around here on the left...

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.600
Yes, so, we can go in here...

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.840
A very good pathway...

00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:44.149
So, here's the building.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.920
The workspace was all burned down,
 during a fire a few years ago.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.160
So, the roof is pretty broken,&nbsp;
and slowly the trees are taking over...

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.835
It's a pretty big space to all the way down&nbsp;
there

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.490
Some concrete structure?

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.275
I don't know how strong or solid it is...

00:02:07.275 --> 00:02:08.729
I guess we have&nbsp;to test?

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:10.865
It looks like there's some work to do.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:18.293
So, yeah, that's the current workspace,
 but&nbsp;we can go in as well!

00:02:18.876 --> 00:02:27.703
Because, yesterday, I made a little pathway,
which is kind&nbsp;of fun and there's a lot of overgrown bushes...

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.097
It's mainly thorns, so you really have to make your&nbsp;way in...

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.736
It could be fun to get in.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.284
Here's the front side of the workspace,
so we made a hole there.

00:02:42.284 --> 00:02:43.774
Well, the hole was already there...

00:02:43.774 --> 00:02:45.715
We just cleaned it.

00:02:45.715 --> 00:02:49.840
And then, here,&nbsp;through the thorns, I made a bit of a path.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.722
Oh yeah, and the camera sometimes&nbsp;has a bit of focusing issues...

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:16.632
Okay, so, right there is another entrance.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.206
So, yeah, as you can see,
 it's fully overgrown, but this is the structure.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.729
Here is another part.

00:03:33.729 --> 00:03:37.360
I don't think it ever&nbsp;had a roof,
but it does have a foundation there.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.360
So, I think that the ideal scenario right now
is that this is all just workspace.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.475
And then, here is the roof.

00:03:47.246 --> 00:03:50.851
I guess I need to watch&nbsp;out 
that those things don't fall on my head.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:54.480
It should be okay?

00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:56.001
We'll do it like&nbsp;this.

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:57.237
At least, we then have it on camera!

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.567
Which could be a cool shot!

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.564
Maybe next&nbsp;time.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.566
And then, here's our little hole out.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.347
So, yeah, that's the workspace!

00:04:15.347 --> 00:04:17.600
There's still some work to do.

00:04:20.788 --> 00:04:22.867
I think this could be a very cool place, because...

00:04:23.415 --> 00:04:24.115
Down there--

00:04:24.115 --> 00:04:25.180
Well, you don't really see it now...

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.500
You have somewhat, and you could have, a nice view!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:35.094
So, now, we go up to the other structure,
 which&nbsp;is going to be the kitchen.

00:04:35.094 --> 00:04:37.686
We go up here through bushes.

00:04:38.769 --> 00:04:42.090
These are basically&nbsp;the two existing structures on the land.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.530
And, I would say they're not very well built...

00:04:50.625 --> 00:04:55.840
So, we have to see if we can&nbsp;renovate them,
 or we have to rebuild them.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.592
That could be the kitchen.

00:04:58.592 --> 00:05:00.000
Also, a lot of&nbsp;thorns here.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.742
We also made a pathway right here.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.600
And, as you can see, underneath there's really ruins.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.520
So, they've been built like over 50 years&nbsp;ago,
 and this is more built on top later.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.836
But, underneath, it could be a super cool&nbsp;place to store food.

00:05:20.294 --> 00:05:24.708
Because of the thick rocks and the granite,
 it keeps everything very cool

00:05:25.604 --> 00:05:29.056
I mean, it could use some cleaning up, but...

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.835
There's another area here.

00:05:38.272 --> 00:05:40.578
It looks lighter on the camera!

00:05:45.431 --> 00:05:47.338
That's the downstairs.

00:05:48.275 --> 00:05:51.858
And then, the top I actually never entered!

00:05:51.858 --> 00:05:54.696
Even&nbsp;before we bought it, because you just couldn't get in...

00:05:54.696 --> 00:05:57.959
Or, at least not quickly, when with the people there.

00:05:57.959 --> 00:06:01.032
So, I started making a pathway to there as well.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.142
Right here, in the forest.

00:06:04.142 --> 00:06:07.974
It's not&nbsp;really a forest, but more like a starting forest.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:17.359
A lot of this burnt down a few years&nbsp;ago with a big fire,
 so that's why you see a&nbsp;lot of young trees now.

00:06:18.338 --> 00:06:24.635
There's actually a lot&nbsp;of acacia trees, which grow super fast!

00:06:24.635 --> 00:06:27.499
But, in a way, they also kind of dominate all the other trees...

00:06:27.499 --> 00:06:32.730
So, in a way, it's cool that they're there,
 but maybe for the long term, not really...

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:34.998
But, we still need to learn more about that.

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:43.741
I was quite surprised, when going into&nbsp;this kitchen.

00:06:43.741 --> 00:06:48.185
Because, I mean, it's also a very rough building.

00:06:49.581 --> 00:06:51.774
It's almost falling apart.

00:06:51.774 --> 00:06:54.072
But, this actually could be very nice, I think.

00:06:54.072 --> 00:06:56.413
I don't know what this flap is.

00:06:56.413 --> 00:07:00.968
Some insulation material put into the wall?

00:07:00.968 --> 00:07:02.152
I don't know.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:10.731
Yeah, so, here could be a&nbsp;nice way to cook.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.757
So, imagine!

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:28.016
Imagine that over here you have a little kitchen.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.944
Something in the fridge...

00:07:32.238 --> 00:07:33.532
Yeah, come for food!

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.179
It could be nice to cook here.

00:07:37.179 --> 00:07:44.919
And then, what I like about&nbsp;this is this window here,
 because it really gives you an overview of the land.

00:07:44.919 --> 00:07:50.400
Where you could grow&nbsp;your vegetables,
 which I think is a nice addition.

00:07:54.278 --> 00:07:56.327
Yeah, so, that was the kitchen&nbsp;structure.

00:07:57.139 --> 00:07:59.211
It's still not the shot...

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:03.613
Let's see now--

00:08:03.613 --> 00:08:04.880
Oops, sorry! The card was full!

00:08:07.055 --> 00:08:09.723
Now, we're going back from the&nbsp;kitchen.

00:08:09.723 --> 00:08:11.723
Towards, uh...

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.090
Just to show you the end of the land.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.091
Yeah, like I said, very bushy...

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:32.611
All right.

00:08:33.486 --> 00:08:36.427
So, I'll have a walk on here,&nbsp;
but maybe i'll just take a run!

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.653
So, yeah, this is the bottom.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:01.370
There's&nbsp;the kitchen.

00:09:01.682 --> 00:09:03.362
It's quite a big piece of land.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.000
That's, I guess, the downside of a big land.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:10.041
You&nbsp;need to run around a lot, to go from A to B.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.004
Currently, we are parked down here, at the&nbsp;bottom

00:09:15.004 --> 00:09:18.240
So, basically, everything here is the land.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:20.910
Hello!

00:09:22.118 --> 00:09:23.506
That's the neighbor.

00:09:23.506 --> 00:09:25.759
Portuguese, but no&nbsp;English.

00:09:25.759 --> 00:09:27.475
I still need to turn some Portuguese.

00:09:29.871 --> 00:09:31.151
So, that's currently the house.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:39.760
And yeah, this is the bottom of the land,&nbsp;
but i realized actually forgot a few things.

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.000
But, maybe I could just--

00:09:42.292 --> 00:09:44.270
Over here, we have an&nbsp;electricity pole.

00:09:45.499 --> 00:09:48.754
I mean, it was already there to provide the neighbors more electricity

00:09:49.608 --> 00:09:52.255
We would need to get it at some point as well.

00:09:53.588 --> 00:09:58.493
But, I figured: ''You can climb in there&nbsp;a bit,
and you might have a better view."

00:10:01.738 --> 00:10:04.298
It's getting a bit narrow for the shoes, so I'll stop here.

00:10:07.572 --> 00:10:09.492
You can see a little bit of the surroundings.

00:10:12.208 --> 00:10:13.568
Overall, it's very green.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.480
Maybe next time, we will go higher.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.500
All right! Let's go to another thing!

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:29.440
This&nbsp;area at the end is probably where we're going to 
set up the Basekamp in the&nbsp;beginning, because it's kind of flat.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:36.320
It's protected, so this means the two&nbsp;
shipping containers would come here.

00:10:38.022 --> 00:10:40.019
You can see more about that in the next&nbsp;time.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:42.588
Well, one thing I wanted to show you...

00:10:44.921 --> 00:10:49.360
The neighbors were actually saying there&nbsp;used
 to be a well, up here in the bushes.

00:10:51.817 --> 00:10:58.023
It had enough water all year round,
 to&nbsp;provide the land with water, which is kind of cool to have.&nbsp;

00:10:58.981 --> 00:11:03.350
But, we also never saw that one before,
because it was just covered in bushes.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:11.371
So, yeah, I did some chopping and some walking in the bushes.

00:11:14.037 --> 00:11:19.786
Then, I made a pathway, and I'm just looking where I was.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:24.956
All right, sorry...

00:11:24.956 --> 00:11:27.893
I had to turn off my camera&nbsp;for a bit,
 because i got a bit confused...

00:11:28.684 --> 00:11:32.443
This whole bush here, which was 
an upcoming forest, was chopped down.

00:11:32.443 --> 00:11:36.190
So, I was calling a bit, to find out why.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.728
It looks pretty rough.

00:11:39.207 --> 00:11:47.088
This wasn't&nbsp;here like yesterday, but apparently someone 
in the neighborhood chops down trees here for his&nbsp;firewood?

00:11:49.608 --> 00:11:51.213
I wasn't really aware of that!

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.574
It looks pretty rough!

00:11:53.574 --> 00:11:56.069
I mean, it kind of changes the landscape...

00:11:56.069 --> 00:12:03.080
But, I guess we need to work out a little bit of 
these things as well with&nbsp;the neighborhood, here on the land.

00:12:05.907 --> 00:12:08.050
Anyway, let's have a look at the water.

00:12:08.362 --> 00:12:11.592
I guess I now also lost my pathway somewhere here?

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.149
But, it doesn't have that many thorns.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.672
So, maybe, we can just go in here?

00:12:24.837 --> 00:12:29.854
There's also&nbsp;a lot of mushrooms in here, at this moment.

00:12:32.612 --> 00:12:35.564
I still need to learn which one&nbsp;you can eat, here in Portugal.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.276
And, then somewhere...

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:39.360
I think it's there!

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.423
So, here's the water!

00:12:50.381 --> 00:12:52.398
Let me take a better shot...

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.741
Sorry for the sound effects.

00:13:06.282 --> 00:13:08.880
So,&nbsp;here's quite a big reservoir of water.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:12.759
It's a bit covered between all the other&nbsp;things.

00:13:13.113 --> 00:13:14.554
Let me throw a stick.

00:13:15.194 --> 00:13:16.063
Yeah, water...

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.440
It just need some cleaning&nbsp;up, before we can even access it.

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:22.742
All right!

00:13:22.742 --> 00:13:23.503
So, that was it!

00:13:23.503 --> 00:13:25.440
The first Project Kamp&nbsp;update video!

00:13:25.836 --> 00:13:29.292
If you want to see more Project Kamp videos,
 make sure to visit our academy!

00:13:29.792 --> 00:13:34.321
If you want to continue to follow this process,
 and see what we're going to do with the land...

00:13:34.321 --> 00:13:35.472
Make&nbsp;sure to subscribe!

00:13:35.472 --> 00:13:40.353
There are a lot of videos and updates coming up,
 to see how we regenerate&nbsp;the land.

00:13:40.353 --> 00:13:41.680
And, how we set up our infrastructure.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:47.575
If you want to help out in some way,
make sure to visit support.projectkamp.com.

00:13:47.575 --> 00:13:49.833
To see how you can help out at this moment!

00:13:50.541 --> 00:13:52.720
Thanks for watching, and see you in the next video!

